This project aimed to extract printed text from images by combining machine learning and OCR techniques.
We utilized Support Vector Machine (SVM) algorithms for classifying and recognizing segmented text regions, followed by Tesseract OCR to extract the textual content from those segments.
The process began with image segmentation to isolate the relevant text areas, after which the SVM model handled recognition tasks.
Tesseract was then applied to convert the segmented images into editable text. The system demonstrated high accuracy, achieving up to 98% in printed text extraction.
This project was completed as part of our final-year academic curriculum, in which our team of three members collaborated on model development, image processing, and performance evaluation.
